mixin () {
  /// Static behavioral documentation for the backend API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Virtual Pay — Backend API\n\nA fun, virtual-only money tracking and prank payment app. No real money is involved; all balances and transfers are simulated game state.\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery method except `getApiDoc` requires a signed (non-anonymous) caller. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n## Registration prerequisite\n\nAccess is gated by the authorization component. A direct API caller must register before any role-guarded call, guarded queries included: call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller. The first caller to initialize becomes `#admin`; every subsequent caller becomes `#user`. An unregistered or anonymous caller receives a trap on guarded endpoints, for example `Unauthorized: Only users can view their balance`. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Authorization\n\nAll wallet, friend, transaction, request, card, and profile data is private to the signed-in caller. Every guarded method checks `#user` permission and traps with `Unauthorized: ...` otherwise. A caller can only read or modify their own wallet, friends, transactions, requests, and card. `getUserProfile` returns only the public view (name, class, roll number, Instagram ID) of another user and never their balance or history. `getLeaderboard` is readable by any signed-in user and exposes only full name, Instagram ID, and balance.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- Amounts are whole fake rupees (`Nat`).\n- Timestamps are nanoseconds from `Time.now()` (signed `Int`).\n- User IDs are `Principal` values.\n- `Direction` is `#sent` or `#received` from the wallet owner's perspective.\n- `RequestStatus` is `#pending`, `#accepted`, or `#declined`.\n- `AddFriendError` is `#notFound`, `#alreadyFriend`, or `#cannotAddSelf`.\n- `TransferError` is `#insufficientBalance { balance }`, `#recipientNotFound`, `#cannotSendToSelf`, or `#invalidAmount`.\n- `RequestError` is `#notFound`, `#notRecipient`, `#alreadyResolved`, or `#insufficientBalance { balance }`.\n- The personal QR payload is the text `vpay:friend:<principal>`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- Onboarding: `createCallerProfile` sets the profile and the starting balance (default 10,000). Call it once; `getCallerProfile` returns null until then.\n- `sendMoney` is atomic: it debits the sender, credits the recipient, and appends a transaction to both histories in one call.\n- `requestMoney` creates a `#pending` request. The recipient sees it via `listIncomingRequests` and resolves it with `acceptRequest` or `declineRequest`; the sender tracks it via `listOutgoingRequests`.\n- Poll `listIncomingRequests` and `listTransactions` to refresh the UI after a transfer.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `sendMoney`, `acceptRequest`, and `declineRequest` are not idempotent: retrying a successful call performs the transfer again. Confirm success before retrying.\n- `createCallerProfile` overwrites the existing profile and does not reset the balance; safe to retry.\n- `saveMyCard` replaces the caller's card; safe to retry.\n- `addFriend` returns `#alreadyFriend` on a repeat and does not duplicate the entry.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Sending more than the current balance returns `#insufficientBalance { balance }` and leaves the balance unchanged.\n- A user cannot send to or add themselves (`#cannotSendToSelf`, `#cannotAddSelf`).\n- `sendMoney` requires the recipient to have an onboarded profile; otherwise it returns `#recipientNotFound`.\n- `acceptRequest` requires the caller to be the request's recipient and the request to still be `#pending`.\n- `getMyQrPayload` returns the caller's own payload; scanning it resolves to the caller and is rejected as self.\n";
  };
};
